The --checkouts file is a directory.  The program dies with an uncaught exception and a stack
trace, and exit status 1.  That is a bug.  The goal files record the current (wrong) behavior, but
only the first line of standard error, because the rest of the stack trace contains line numbers
within the JDK and within libraries, which vary from version to version.

The program should instead report the problem in a one-line message that names the file and
contains no stack trace, as it does for a nonexistent --checkouts file (see
list-nonexistent-checkouts-file).
